      <div type="clause" n="Prol.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> Prol.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="278" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis is seo gerædnys<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1"/>, þe Cnut ciningc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.2"/>, ealles Englalandes ciningc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.3"/> ⁊ Dena cining<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.4"/> mid his witena geþeahte gerædde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5"/>, Gode to lofe ⁊ him sylfum to cynescipe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6"/> ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star2"/> to þearfe; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wæs on ðære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.7"/> halgan midewintres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.8"/> tide on Winceastre.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="278" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis is seo gerednes, þe Cnut cyni<hi rend="italic">n</hi>gc mid his witena geþeahte geredde, Gode to lofe ⁊ hym sylfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to cynescipe ⁊ to þearfe; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wæs on ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1-3"/> halgan middewintres tid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1-3"/> on Winceastre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="279" ed="#liebermann"/>Hęc sunt instituta Cnudi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1-2"/> regis Anglorum, Danorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star2-2"/>, Norwegarum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.2-2"/> uenerando sapientum eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.3-2"/> consilio ad laudem et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.4-2"/> gloriam Dei et suam regalitatem et commune<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5-2"/> commodum habita in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6-2"/> sancto natali Domini apud Wintoniam.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star3-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="279" ed="#liebermann"/>Hęc est institutio, quam Cnud<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5-3"/> rex cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6-4"/> consilio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.7-3"/> principum suorum sapientium ad laudem Dei et honorem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.8-2"/> sui ipsius et profectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.9"/> totius regni<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.10"/> cui preerat instituit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="279" ed="#liebermann"/>Hec est consiliacio, quam Cnutus rex meditacionem suorum sapientum consiliatus est, Deo ad laudem et sibimet ad regiam dignitatem et expeditionem; hoc autem factum est in natali Domini apud Wintoniam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.2"/><pb n="154" ed="#robertson"/>Ðis is seo gerædnys þe Cnut ciningc, ealles Englalandes ciningc ⁊ Dena cining<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.3"/>, mid his witena geþeahte gerædde, Gode to lofe ⁊ him sylfum to cynescipe ⁊ [folce]<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.4"/> to þearfe; ⁊ þæt wæs on ðære halgan midewintres tide on Winceastre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="232" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ðis is seo gerædnys þe Cnut ciningc, ealles Englalandes ciningc and Dena cining, mid his witena geþeahte gerædde, Gode to lofe and him sylfum to cynescipe and to þearfe; and þæt wæs on ðære halgan midewintres tide on Winceastre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="278" ed="#liebermann"/><hi rend="italic">Prolog</hi>. Dies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.1"/> ist der Beschluss, welchen König Cnut, König von ganz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.2"/> England und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.3"/> Dänenkönig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.4"/> mit Beistimmung seiner Witan beschloss, Gott zum Preise und sich selbst zur königlichen Ehre und zum Nutzen (dem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.5"/> Volke <hi rend="italic">Ld Quadr</hi>.); und dies geschah an dem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.6"/> heiligen Weihnachtsfeste in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.7"/> Winchester.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_Prol.lnote.de.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Prologue. This is the ordinance which King Cnut, king of all England and king of the Danes, decreed with the counsel of his witan, to the praise of God and to his own royal dignity and benefit (to the people, Ld Quadr.); and that was at the holy Christmas season at Winchester.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="155" ed="#robertson"/>This is the ordinance which King Canute, King of all England and King of the Danes, determined upon with the advice of his Councillors, to the glory of God and for the furtherance of his own royal authority and for his [people's]<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.n.1"/> benefit; and that was during the holy Christmas<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.n.2"/> season at Winchester<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_Prol.robnote.n.3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="462" ed="#whitelock"/>This is the ordinance which King Cnut<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#ICn_Prol.whinote.n.5"/> determined with the advice of his councillors, for the praise of God and for his own royal dignity and benefit; and it took place at the holy Christmas season at Winchester,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="233" ed="#rabin-doml"/>This is the decree which King Cnut, king of all England and king of the Danes, decided upon on the advice of his councilors, for the glory of God and his own sovereignty and the common welfare; and that was during the holy Christmas season at Winchester.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="278, 279"><ref target="clause:IIEg_Prol">II Eg Prol.</ref>; <ref target="clause:Cn1020_4">Cn 1020 4</ref>; <ref target="clause:IIEg_Prol">II Eg Pr.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Eg. Prol. | Vgl. Cn. 1020, 4 | II Eg. Pr.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_Inscr">I Cn Inscr.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_Prol">II Eg Prol.</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn Pr.: II Eg. Pr</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘⁊ to þearfe’ in G after ‘to cynescipe’; Ld adds ‘folc’. Liebermann compares II Eg Prol.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 279, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 232 / 233, October 2026 (was “Đis:; Đis”, now “Ðis:; Ðis”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Manuscripts: A = London, British Library, Harley MS 55, fols. 5r–7v; B = Cambridge, Corpus Christi College MS 383, pp. 43–47; G = London, British Library, Cotton MS Nero A.i, fols. 3r–16r.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Ðis: A precedes this with Ðis is seo gerednes, þe Cnut cyning, ealles Englalandes cyningc and Dena cyningc and Norþrigena cyningc, gerædde, and his witan, Gode to lofe and him sylfum to cynescipe and to þearfe, rade swa hwæðer swa man wille.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ealles . . . cining: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ðære: ðam A</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">the holy Christmas season: Although meetings of the royal council often occurred at Christmas, the particular assembly at which this code was issued has not been identified.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Beginn von Hs. Cotton Nero A I, um</hi> 1070. <hi rend="italic">Verglichen mit</hi> Ld (<hi rend="italic">Lambarde Αρχαιονομια</hi>), <hi rend="italic">der f.</hi> 110, 120 <hi rend="italic">mehrere Hss. zu benutzen erklärt</hi> [<hi rend="italic">nämlich</hi> A, <hi rend="italic">seltener</hi> G, B, <hi rend="italic">vereinzelt auch</hi> (?) eine verlorene.]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Beginning of MS Cotton Nero A I, c. 1070. Collated with Ld (Lambarde, Αρχαιονομια), who says (f. 110, 120) that he uses several MSS [namely A, less often G, B, occasionally also (?) a lost one.]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nes <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nes Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyning <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyning Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cynning ⁊ Norþrigena cyning <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">aus Inscr. A's?</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cynning ⁊ Norþrigena cyning Ld [from the Inscr. of A?]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gered <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gered Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-scippe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-scippe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">folc [<hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> folce] <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld; vgl. Quadr. Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">folc [read folce] added by Ld; cf. Quadr. Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">midw. tid <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">midw. tid Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wintanceastre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wintanceastre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cnuti <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> Canuti <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> Kanuti <hi rend="italic">Br;</hi> Knutonis <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnuti T; Canuti Hk; Kanuti Br; Knutonis Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star2-2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Swenorum <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Swenorum added by Lond.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gor. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> Norwiganorum <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gor. T; Norwiganorum Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. e. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. e. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et g. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et g. lacking in Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">regni <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">regni added by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. W. in s. n. D. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. W. in s. n. D. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.star3-2" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">diligenter ac fideliter ex Anglico [ex A. <hi rend="italic">nur Lond</hi>] in Latinum compendiosa breuitate quante [<hi rend="italic">so</hi>] decuit simplicitate translata [<hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> in L. t. co. b. cum si. lucida <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi>], quadam Latinitatis elegantia [q. L. e. <hi rend="italic">nur Lond</hi>], uelud quisbusdam [<hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> suis <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi>] asteriscis et obelis super Anglicum [et o. s. A. <hi rend="italic">nur Lond; fehlt übr.</hi>] illustrata, in quo [<hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> unde <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi>] quantam rerum et uerborum affinitatem [uel indempnitatem <hi rend="italic">nur Co Or</hi>] paucorum adiectione uel omissione curauerim, facile sobrius lector agnoscet. (Secuntur et aliorum iura regum plurimorum, de quibus teneri liceat quicquid ista contemplatione non discrepat <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi>). Capitula: <hi rend="italic">d. i. Rubrikenliste</hi> [<hi rend="italic">gedruckt Liebermann</hi> Quadripartitus <hi rend="italic">S.</hi> 90—99], <hi rend="italic">wohl ohne Angelsächsische Vorlage. Einschaltung des Quadripartitus.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">diligenter ac fideliter ex Anglico [ex A. only Lond] in Latinum compendiosa breuitate quante [sic] decuit simplicitate translata [thus Lond; in L. t. co. b. cum si. lucida the rest], quadam Latinitatis elegantia [q. L. e. only Lond], uelud quisbusdam [thus Lond; suis the rest] asteriscis et obelis super Anglicum [et o. s. A. only Lond; lacking in the rest] illustrata, in quo [Lond; unde the rest] quantam rerum et uerborum affinitatem [uel indempnitatem only Co Or] paucorum adiectione uel omissione curauerim, facile sobrius lector agnoscet. (Secuntur et aliorum iura regum plurimorum, de quibus teneri liceat quicquid ista contemplatione non discrepat lacking in Lond). Capitula: i.e. list of rubrics [printed Liebermann Quadripartitus pp. 90—99], probably without an Anglo-Saxon original. An interpolation by the Quadripartitus.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">statt</hi> Hec — expeditionem <hi rend="italic">folgt dem Prolog der</hi> Inst. Cn. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">instead of Hec — expeditionem, Cb follows the prologue of the Inst. Cn.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Chn. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Chn. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> secundum <hi rend="italic">oder lies</hi> cum meditacione</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply secundum or read cum meditacione</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cnut <hi rend="italic">Rl Lb Jo Va;</hi> Cnutus <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> Chnutus <hi rend="italic">S Pl</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut Rl Lb Jo Va; Cnutus Cb; Chnutus S Pl</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.6-4" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb Lb S Ct Jo Va</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb Lb S Ct Jo Va</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.7-3" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">decreto <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">decreto Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ecclesie et dignitatem <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb aus Consil.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ecclesie et dignitatem added by Cb from the Consil.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad utilitatem <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad utilitatem Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">279</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sui <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sui added by Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">278</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D lässt den Pro fort, weil er ihn in die Insc hineinarbeitete. Die Insc in AC benutzt den Pro, ebenso Ps Cn for Pro</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">D omits the Pro because he worked it into the Insc. The Insc in AC uses the Pro, as does Ps Cn for Pro</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. Cn 1027 Insc c. AIC lassen den Titel fort, weil sie ihn schon in Insc gaben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> Cn 1027 Insc c. AIC omit the title because they had already given it in the Insc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Königstitel 5a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Königstitel 5a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. Insc⁸</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> Insc⁸</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folce</hi> stand im Archetyp vielleicht am Rande; Cn 1020, 8 bezeugt die Authentizität. Vielleicht hierher <hi rend="italic">þeode þearfe</hi> 1a D</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">folce</hi> perhaps stood in the margin in the archetype; Cn 1020, 8 attests its authenticity. <hi rend="italic">þeode þearfe</hi> 1a D perhaps belongs here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. zu <hi rend="italic">tid</hi> neutr. <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> Genus 7.—Über das Jahr <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. on <hi rend="italic">tid</hi> as a neuter <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> Genus 7.—On the year <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. mein <hi rend="italic">National assembly</hi> p. 47. 82</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. my <hi rend="italic">National assembly</hi> p. 47. 82</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_Prol.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q's <hi rend="italic">per obelos ct asteriscos</hi> ist Zitat aus Hieronymus ep. 112.—Q's <hi rend="italic">Capitula</hi> findet man <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. I 535</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q's <hi rend="italic">per obelos ct asteriscos</hi> is a quotation from Hieronymus ep. 112.—Q's <hi rend="italic">Capitula</hi> will be found <hi rend="italic">above</hi> I 535</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G and A both read simply <hi rend="italic">to þearfe</hi>, cf. <hi rend="italic">sibimet ad regiam dignitatem et expeditionem</hi>, Cons.; Ld however reads: <hi rend="italic">folc to þearfe</hi>, cf. <hi rend="italic">ad commune commodum</hi>, Q; <hi rend="italic">ad profectum totius regni cui preerat</hi>, Inst. Liebermann suggests that <hi rend="italic">folce</hi> may have been a marginal reading in the archetype. The phrase <hi rend="italic">him silfum to cynescype ⁊ to þearfe</hi> appears also in II Edg. Pre. D, where the other MSS read <hi rend="italic">eallum his leodscipe to þearfe</hi>, cf. IV Edg. 2, 1 <hi rend="italic">a</hi>; <hi rend="italic">to ealles folces þ.</hi>, Cn. 1020, 8; <hi rend="italic">þeode þearfe</hi>, I Cn. 1, D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann (<hi rend="italic">National Assembly in the A.S. Period</hi>, p. 49) gives a list of 20 assemblies which met at Christmas.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For a list of assemblies held at Winchester see Liebermann, <hi rend="italic">op. cit.</hi> p. 47. Q here contains an addition relating to the translation of the ordinance from English into Latin.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>Ðis</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G; no preamble in D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>cining</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ealles…cining</hi> om. A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>folce</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">folc</hi> Ld, om. G, A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ICn_Prol.whinote.n.5" n="5" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">462</biblScope></bibl><label>Cnut</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The Nero text adds here: “king of all England and king of the Danes”; but as without this the prologue is exactly in the form of that of II Edgar, I suspect this of being an accretion.</seg></note>
